NotchLite is a modified distribution of Ada, based on upstream revision
5a1e17f040672a71685872b1b234e01d02a47bb5. Modified 2026-11-26.
Changes: separate application identity/storage, opt-in first-run settings,
mascot timer lifecycle, animation interval, measurement tooling and project docs.
Original attribution and third-party notices are retained below.
Further NotchLite changes: reentrant window shutdown, isolated startup setting,
UTF-16 input, editor focus lifecycle, web-link validation and weather cancellation.
Version 0.1.2 also changes first-run publication, hidden-window rendering,
explicit panel opening and bounded clipboard paste. Development-only Ponytail
guidance is under .agents/skills with its separate MIT notices.
Version 0.1.3 adds shared native appearance presets, persistence feedback and
fallible settings reloads that preserve the active configuration on read errors.
Version 0.1.4 adds an opt-in native GDI clock window, independent of the notch.
The clock implementation is an original addition to this fork.
Version 0.1.5 adds a native icon navigation bar, local keyboard page switching
and the Rose palette. Noci Share is a visual reference; no Noci code or assets
are included. The mobile file-sharing backend was not implemented in 0.1.5.
Version 0.1.6 adds an opt-in LAN TLS server, temporary QR enrollment, PC consent,
bounded file streams and original native Android/iPhone companion applications.
This is an experimental addition, not a port of Noci/NotchPixel code.
Rust dependency license/notice texts are distributed under licenses/rust;
mobile dependency notices are under companion. Preserve these with binaries.
Version 0.1.7 adds opt-in secondary-monitor GDI panels, a local Codex daemon
client, process metrics and a metadata-only Windows communications detector.
In version 0.1.7, audio capture and AI call processing remained disabled.
Version 0.1.8 adds explicitly confirmed application process-loopback capture,
local whisper.cpp transcription and an optional text-only bridge for an active
assistant. whisper.cpp and Whisper model dependencies are separate optional
downloads with their original MIT notices; see docs/CALL-TRANSCRIPTION.md.
The current embedded Codex Desktop runtime is not connected by this bridge.

